WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.151
(organ music)

00:00:02.151 --> 00:00:04.488
- [Voiceover] The green
fur, the gyrating belly,

00:00:04.488 --> 00:00:07.106
the party horn nose.
This is Phillie Phanatic,

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:10.189
mascot for the Philadelphia Phillies.

00:00:11.225 --> 00:00:13.643
The Phillies' mascot is maybe
the wackiest of them all,

00:00:13.643 --> 00:00:16.611
at least in the MLB, but
it wasn't always that way.

00:00:16.611 --> 00:00:19.782
In the 1970s, the Phillies
had Philadelphia Phil

00:00:19.782 --> 00:00:22.315
and Philadelphia Phillis,
a pair of mascots

00:00:22.315 --> 00:00:24.305
straight out of the 18th century,

00:00:24.305 --> 00:00:26.301
and they were, well, boring.

00:00:26.301 --> 00:00:28.627
(record scratching)
So the Phillies pivoted.

00:00:28.627 --> 00:00:30.217
They commissioned Bonnie and Wayde,

00:00:30.217 --> 00:00:31.628
two Muppet makers who had worked alongside

00:00:31.628 --> 00:00:33.802
puppet mastermind Jim Henson.

00:00:33.802 --> 00:00:35.778
The Phillies decided to
create a family-friendly,

00:00:35.778 --> 00:00:39.271
attention-grabbing mascot,
and on April 25, 1978

00:00:39.271 --> 00:00:42.174
the Phillie Phanatic made
his triumphant debut.

00:00:42.174 --> 00:00:44.332
All six feet of green fur made
its way out onto the field

00:00:44.332 --> 00:00:45.948
to roaring applause.

00:00:45.948 --> 00:00:48.698
(crowd cheering)

00:00:50.546 --> 00:00:53.323
38 years later, the
big, green, ATV riding,

00:00:53.323 --> 00:00:55.132
Super Soaker wielding Phanatic

00:00:55.132 --> 00:00:57.023
is still making the crowds go wild.

00:00:57.023 --> 00:00:59.769
(clapping and cheering)

00:00:59.769 --> 00:01:01.111
So all you Phillies fans,

00:01:01.111 --> 00:01:03.196
give it up for the Phillie Phanatic.

00:01:03.196 --> 00:01:06.363
(exciting drum music)

